xnu 0150: try every QUP4 pad assignment, and probe the IRQ line

The device tree names the four QUP4 pads (gpio16-19) but not which QUP signal
each one carries, and 0148/0149 show that neither the assumed order (16 clk,
17 mosi, 18 miso, 19 cs) nor the mosi/miso swap gets anything back from the
part. One of the four pads is CS; the other three are clk, mosi and miso in
some order. Try all 24 assignments, each after a real IOVDD power cycle, with
MISO sampled on both clock edges, writing the 0xAA boot-option handshake first
and reading it back. The first mapping that answers is the wiring.

Also read the IRQ pad with an internal pull-down: a part that is powered and
out of reset drives its interrupt line high against it, while a part without
AVDD leaves the pull-down in charge. That separates "no answer because the
transport is wrong" from "no answer because the part is not powered".

